@@ -29,3 +29,7 @@ Closing the last game tab releases presence; if the phone cannot notify the serv
 Set **Number of winners** in quiz settings (default 3). Like the questions, this setting is copied into each game when its lobby starts. Every accepted pick replaces both the choice and the server-measured time since the round opened. At **End quiz**, scores and places are finalized for all players, including disconnected ones. Each correct final pick earns one point; lower total time on correct answers breaks ties, with join order as the fallback for an exact tie.
 
 **Top N** awards the first N places with points. **Draw** keeps everyone above the point cutoff and randomly fills the remaining prizes from the players at the cutoff, without considering speed. Each draw is independent, so it can repeat a previous result. **Reset winners** clears only the awards, not the standings. Both the leaderboard and personal result screens stay subscribed after the game ends.
+
+## Question timer
+
+Set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** in quiz settings; leave both at zero for untimed questions. Only the projector shows the countdown. Each round gets its own deadline when it opens, and **Finish** still works before time runs out. The timer is local to the quiz and is not exported.
